1
00:01:43,185 --> 00:01:45,785
KEEP QUIET

2
00:01:45,865 --> 00:01:49,505
SURGICAL WARD

3
00:01:53,625 --> 00:01:54,505
Sir.

4
00:02:12,785 --> 00:02:13,705
Sir.

5
00:02:16,145 --> 00:02:17,385
What are you doing here?

6
00:02:17,945 --> 00:02:20,945
You're getting discharged today.
I came to help you pack.

7
00:02:22,705 --> 00:02:23,825
Come on.

8
00:02:30,465 --> 00:02:31,425
<i>PARADOX THINKING</i>
<i>IN CRIMINAL INVESTIGATIONS</i>

9
00:02:31,505 --> 00:02:32,385
BY RAN FANGXU

10
00:02:34,265 --> 00:02:35,785
Why are you reading that?

11
00:02:35,865 --> 00:02:37,705
Just brushing up.

12
00:02:40,345 --> 00:02:41,345
Hey.

13
00:02:42,505 --> 00:02:43,425
Give it back.

14
00:02:46,145 --> 00:02:48,745
I wrote that two years ago
when I didn't know any better.

15
00:02:48,825 --> 00:02:50,385
It's all just theory.

16
00:02:51,625 --> 00:02:53,305
That's what I used to think too.

17
00:02:53,385 --> 00:02:55,025
But now,

18
00:02:55,625 --> 00:02:59,225
your so-called theory
actually holds up in practice.

19
00:02:59,305 --> 00:03:00,145
It's helpful.

20
00:03:04,265 --> 00:03:05,785
By the way, sir,

21
00:03:05,865 --> 00:03:08,105
what are you planning to do
after you're discharged?

22
00:03:13,945 --> 00:03:16,745
Can I stay on
with the Criminal Department?

23
00:03:18,185 --> 00:03:19,465
Of course.

24
00:03:20,465 --> 00:03:22,025
You got injured on duty.

25
00:03:22,105 --> 00:03:24,305
The team will make room for you.

26
00:03:26,105 --> 00:03:27,105
Then I'll stay.

27
00:03:27,865 --> 00:03:28,785
Good.

28
00:03:38,745 --> 00:03:40,065
What about Xiaohe?

29
00:03:40,945 --> 00:03:42,745
I need to look after her,

30
00:03:42,825 --> 00:03:44,345
and I have cases to crack.

31
00:03:44,985 --> 00:03:46,785
Cases? What case?

32
00:03:48,425 --> 00:03:51,305
Do you really think Xu Meng is dead?

33
00:03:54,345 --> 00:03:57,385
I've been thinking. A case
that dragged on for five years,

34
00:03:57,465 --> 00:04:00,145
and suddenly it gets wrapped up
in three days. That's way too smooth.

35
00:04:00,745 --> 00:04:03,425
Could there be a possibility that Xu Meng

36
00:04:03,505 --> 00:04:06,145
got away from Wu Shanlong a long time ago,

37
00:04:06,225 --> 00:04:08,945
and he just left her shoes behind?

38
00:04:09,025 --> 00:04:09,985
That's possible.

39
00:04:11,065 --> 00:04:13,745
As long as we have
solid evidence and leads,

40
00:04:14,345 --> 00:04:16,865
I'll go to Director Zou
and ask to reopen the case.

41
00:04:17,585 --> 00:04:18,624
Director Zou?

42
00:04:18,705 --> 00:04:19,825
Why him?

43
00:04:19,905 --> 00:04:22,105
Shouldn't we report to Captain Feng?

44
00:04:23,705 --> 00:04:26,105
Captain Feng retired last week.

45
00:04:29,065 --> 00:04:30,465
So that means…

46
00:04:31,305 --> 00:04:32,545
You brat.

47
00:04:36,505 --> 00:04:37,785
Captain Ran.

48
00:04:38,785 --> 00:04:40,105
Come on. Don't do that.

49
00:04:41,025 --> 00:04:42,465
You,

50
00:04:42,545 --> 00:04:45,425
get back to work. Don't waste time here.

51
00:04:45,505 --> 00:04:47,625
-Go.
-About Xu Meng's case?

52
00:04:49,065 --> 00:04:50,225
No rush.

53
00:04:50,305 --> 00:04:51,145
I'll think it through some more.

54
00:04:53,625 --> 00:04:55,865
-I'm going then.
-Go on.

55
00:04:55,945 --> 00:04:57,385
Hurry.

56
00:05:13,905 --> 00:05:18,025
FOUR MONTHS LATER, EARLY WINTER

57
00:05:18,105 --> 00:05:20,065
The theft ring is hiding
in the urban village.

58
00:05:20,145 --> 00:05:21,945
If we lock it down,
we can take them all in one sweep.

59
00:05:22,025 --> 00:05:23,545
There are so few of us.

60
00:05:23,625 --> 00:05:24,745
How are we supposed to seal it off?

61
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:25,945
What about the northeast corner?

62
00:05:26,025 --> 00:05:27,385
How do we block that? You tell me.

63
00:05:36,545 --> 00:05:37,865
Is the arrest plan ready?

64
00:05:37,945 --> 00:05:40,025
We are working it out.

65
00:05:40,545 --> 00:05:42,665
The urban-village area is complicated.

66
00:05:44,825 --> 00:05:45,865
Where's Ran Fangxu?

67
00:05:47,585 --> 00:05:48,825
He was here just now.

68
00:05:52,625 --> 00:05:54,985
Captain Ran. Captain Ran.

69
00:05:55,065 --> 00:05:55,945
Wake up.

70
00:05:57,865 --> 00:05:59,145
Captain Ran. Director Zou is here.

71
00:06:00,385 --> 00:06:01,225
Director Zou,

72
00:06:01,305 --> 00:06:03,585
I pulled an all-nighter last night.
I'm so tired. Can't keep my eyes open.

73
00:06:05,625 --> 00:06:06,625
I'm here.

74
00:06:10,825 --> 00:06:12,665
Get out. Go wake yourself up outside.

75
00:06:13,585 --> 00:06:14,385
Yes, sir.

76
00:06:17,905 --> 00:06:19,465
This group of thieves
stole 1.5 million in cash

77
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:22,505
from the Railway Administration
and is hiding in the urban village.

78
00:06:22,585 --> 00:06:24,625
The tricky part is the northeast corner.

79
00:06:24,705 --> 00:06:27,825
In this corner, there are over
a dozen paths of all kinds

80
00:06:27,905 --> 00:06:30,145
and plenty of hidden openings like these.

81
00:06:31,145 --> 00:06:32,585
We've tried multiple plans,

82
00:06:32,665 --> 00:06:35,625
but still can't fully block
Luandongzi's escape routes.

83
00:06:43,065 --> 00:06:44,425
Director Zou,

84
00:06:44,505 --> 00:06:47,145
should we call in armed police for backup?

85
00:07:00,425 --> 00:07:01,265
Director Zou.

86
00:07:02,905 --> 00:07:04,625
Leave the northeast corner to me.

87
00:07:05,545 --> 00:07:08,705
-Problem solved!
-All good then!

88
00:07:08,785 --> 00:07:10,385
-That'd be great.
-Good then.

89
00:07:11,385 --> 00:07:13,625
If your captain is willing
to stake his life on it,

90
00:07:14,425 --> 00:07:16,345
-then it's settled.
-Wait.

91
00:07:16,425 --> 00:07:17,665
-Zhao Jie.
-Yes, sir.

92
00:07:18,185 --> 00:07:20,385
-Put that into the plan.
-Don't.

93
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:22,145
Director Zou,

94
00:07:22,225 --> 00:07:24,345
I never said I'd stake my life.

95
00:07:26,065 --> 00:07:27,425
-Did he or not?
-He did.

96
00:07:29,945 --> 00:07:32,465
SOLIDARITY

97
00:07:42,185 --> 00:07:43,505
We're short one. Just waiting on you.

98
00:07:43,585 --> 00:07:44,625
Hurry up.

99
00:07:52,585 --> 00:07:53,865
Has Captain Ran
gone to the northeast corner?

100
00:07:53,945 --> 00:07:55,185
He has. Don't worry.

101
00:08:10,465 --> 00:08:12,945
So sorry. Sorry.

102
00:08:18,665 --> 00:08:19,385
Move.

103
00:08:20,425 --> 00:08:21,625
Stop!

104
00:08:23,665 --> 00:08:24,545
-Cut him off over there.
-Go.

105
00:08:25,825 --> 00:08:27,505
-Stop.
-Stop.

106
00:08:28,105 --> 00:08:29,225
-Don't run.
-Watch out.

107
00:08:29,305 --> 00:08:30,145
Don't run.

108
00:08:49,665 --> 00:08:51,425
Two of you, go around and box him in.

109
00:08:58,745 --> 00:09:00,745
No one is stopping me.

110
00:09:08,145 --> 00:09:09,905
<i>He walked right into it. Easy.</i>

111
00:09:09,985 --> 00:09:10,985
<i>Don't scratch my car.</i>

112
00:09:15,625 --> 00:09:16,305
POLICE

113
00:09:16,385 --> 00:09:17,225
Get out.

114
00:09:18,705 --> 00:09:20,065
Out of the car.

115
00:09:20,145 --> 00:09:21,225
Don't shoot.

116
00:09:21,305 --> 00:09:22,625
I surrender.

117
00:09:22,705 --> 00:09:24,425
-Take him!
-I surrender.

118
00:09:25,505 --> 00:09:26,265
Ow!

119
00:09:26,345 --> 00:09:27,345
Cuff him.

120
00:09:27,425 --> 00:09:29,105
-Easy.
-Don't move.

121
00:09:29,185 --> 00:09:30,465
Take him away.

122
00:09:31,985 --> 00:09:33,225
Officer,

123
00:09:33,305 --> 00:09:34,585
I have something to report.

124
00:09:34,665 --> 00:09:35,705
I can help.

125
00:09:35,785 --> 00:09:38,185
The property manager
of Yuanlongli, Qian Dajun.

126
00:09:38,265 --> 00:09:40,545
He's bad news.

127
00:09:40,625 --> 00:09:41,705
-Take him back for interrogation.
-Yes, sir.

128
00:09:41,785 --> 00:09:42,985
-Officer! Trust me!
-Move.

129
00:09:43,065 --> 00:09:44,345
Trust me!

130
00:09:44,425 --> 00:09:45,985
-Move.
-Trust me!

131
00:09:46,065 --> 00:09:47,105
I can help!

132
00:09:48,545 --> 00:09:49,825
Captain Ran,

133
00:09:49,905 --> 00:09:52,545
next time you have
something like this, call me in.

134
00:09:52,625 --> 00:09:55,345
I don't often get to play cop like this.

135
00:09:55,425 --> 00:09:56,785
-Thank you, Sun.
-Not at all.

136
00:09:56,865 --> 00:09:58,225
-Appreciate it, Captain Sun.
-Of course.

137
00:09:58,305 --> 00:09:59,585
We couldn't have
pulled this off without you.

138
00:09:59,665 --> 00:10:00,745
Come.

139
00:10:00,825 --> 00:10:02,665
-Good work.
-No problem.

140
00:10:04,185 --> 00:10:05,705
MR. ZHANG

141
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,585
Hello, Mr. Zhang?

142
00:10:11,305 --> 00:10:12,345
I'm so sorry, Mr. Zhang.

143
00:10:12,425 --> 00:10:14,025
Please calm down. I'll handle it.

144
00:10:14,105 --> 00:10:15,105
I'll deal with it right away.

145
00:10:15,185 --> 00:10:21,505
NEIGHBORHOOD EAR CLEANING

146
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:33,225
CANDESARTAN TABLETS

147
00:10:46,505 --> 00:10:49,065
Mister, are you from this neighborhood?

148
00:10:50,585 --> 00:10:51,745
No.

149
00:10:52,785 --> 00:10:54,425
You look familiar.

150
00:10:56,625 --> 00:10:58,305
Back in 1997, I came to ask about

151
00:10:59,345 --> 00:11:01,185
your brother and his daughter
who went missing.

152
00:11:05,745 --> 00:11:07,345
I remember now.

153
00:11:07,425 --> 00:11:09,185
You're that police officer.

154
00:11:09,985 --> 00:11:13,105
Officer, any news about my niece?

155
00:11:17,065 --> 00:11:19,145
It doesn't look good.

156
00:11:19,705 --> 00:11:22,465
That poor girl has had a hard life.

157
00:11:22,545 --> 00:11:26,025
She used to have someone
she was going to marry.

158
00:11:26,105 --> 00:11:27,345
He was from out of town.

159
00:11:27,425 --> 00:11:29,225
He came to Weiyang a few times.

160
00:11:29,305 --> 00:11:30,545
He's from a decent family.

161
00:11:31,305 --> 00:11:33,145
If they'd gotten married,

162
00:11:33,225 --> 00:11:35,785
things might've turned out differently.

163
00:11:36,705 --> 00:11:37,945
She had a boyfriend?

164
00:11:38,025 --> 00:11:39,145
Why didn't you mention that before?

165
00:11:39,225 --> 00:11:41,785
They lost touch a long time ago.

166
00:11:41,865 --> 00:11:43,305
My brother was to blame.

167
00:11:43,385 --> 00:11:45,385
He didn't approve of him
and wouldn't let them be together.

168
00:11:45,465 --> 00:11:48,025
He forced them apart.

169
00:11:50,265 --> 00:11:52,505
Do you remember his name?

170
00:11:52,585 --> 00:11:53,865
What's the name?

171
00:11:54,385 --> 00:11:55,745
It was something nice.

172
00:11:56,345 --> 00:11:58,145
What's his name again?

173
00:11:58,745 --> 00:12:01,345
Qiming. Wan Qiming.

174
00:12:02,145 --> 00:12:03,225
Wan Qiming.

175
00:12:04,465 --> 00:12:06,625
What did he look like?

176
00:12:08,225 --> 00:12:11,345
Wait. I have a photo of him.

177
00:12:11,425 --> 00:12:12,345
Let me show you.

178
00:12:22,505 --> 00:12:24,825
This one. This one here.
The one with glasses.

179
00:12:26,265 --> 00:12:27,345
This?

180
00:12:27,425 --> 00:12:28,585
The man with glasses.

181
00:12:29,745 --> 00:12:32,025
<i>The person who hired you,</i>
<i>what's their name?</i>

182
00:12:32,105 --> 00:12:33,385
<i>What do they look like?</i>

183
00:12:33,465 --> 00:12:34,505
<i>A man.</i>

184
00:12:35,225 --> 00:12:37,705
He looks about 25 or 26.

185
00:12:37,785 --> 00:12:39,425
Tall.

186
00:12:39,505 --> 00:12:40,945
Wears glasses.

187
00:12:41,025 --> 00:12:42,305
Side-parted hair.

188
00:12:42,385 --> 00:12:44,265
<i>Looks well-mannered.</i>

189
00:12:49,505 --> 00:12:52,105
USE WITH CARE, ECO-RECYCLE

190
00:12:53,865 --> 00:12:54,705
Let's do it now.

191
00:12:56,225 --> 00:12:57,105
Are you sure?

192
00:12:59,985 --> 00:13:01,705
Who the heck are you?

193
00:13:02,585 --> 00:13:04,465
Do you know who my boss is?

194
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:07,825
Who?

195
00:13:08,625 --> 00:13:09,905
You.

196
00:13:09,985 --> 00:13:11,465
Get lost.

197
00:13:19,745 --> 00:13:20,825
Let's go home and have dumplings.

198
00:13:20,905 --> 00:13:22,065
You're home.

199
00:13:27,105 --> 00:13:28,265
My goodness.

200
00:13:30,145 --> 00:13:32,185
-Sir.
-Green hair. Panda eyes.

201
00:13:32,945 --> 00:13:34,585
Torn pants. A dog collar.

202
00:13:34,665 --> 00:13:37,705
I'm raising a kid, not some freak.

203
00:13:37,785 --> 00:13:39,785
He Yuanhang, what did you promise me?

204
00:13:39,865 --> 00:13:41,385
If I'd known, I would've gone
to the provincial capital with my mom.

205
00:13:42,745 --> 00:13:44,025
You think I don't keep my word?

206
00:13:44,105 --> 00:13:45,345
I used to just be your dad.

207
00:13:45,425 --> 00:13:47,745
Now I'm playing both parents.

208
00:13:47,825 --> 00:13:49,105
Look at you.

209
00:13:49,185 --> 00:13:50,945
Dye your hair today, tattoo tomorrow.

210
00:13:51,025 --> 00:13:52,345
What's next, drugs?

211
00:13:52,425 --> 00:13:54,025
You're a student, you know that?

212
00:13:54,105 --> 00:13:55,065
School is for idiots.

213
00:13:55,145 --> 00:13:56,225
I'm doing rock.

214
00:13:56,305 --> 00:13:57,585
That's real rock spirit.

215
00:14:03,545 --> 00:14:05,025
Rock spirit, my foot.

216
00:14:05,105 --> 00:14:06,945
More like rock nutcase.

217
00:14:08,185 --> 00:14:09,665
And she still has the nerve
to eat my dumplings?

218
00:14:17,025 --> 00:14:20,305
What's wrong with her?
Am I pushing her too hard?

219
00:14:25,265 --> 00:14:26,265
Take it easy.

220
00:14:26,865 --> 00:14:27,745
I'm not drinking.

221
00:14:29,705 --> 00:14:31,905
Teenagers are like this, right?

222
00:14:33,825 --> 00:14:35,105
Anyway,

223
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:38,665
Xiaohe may be rebellious, but she's smart.

224
00:14:38,745 --> 00:14:42,105
She scored over 95 in every subject
on the mock exam.

225
00:14:44,385 --> 00:14:46,345
Her homeroom teacher told me.

226
00:14:47,305 --> 00:14:48,745
MR. ZHANG

227
00:14:50,225 --> 00:14:51,705
Hello, Mr. Zhang?

228
00:14:52,505 --> 00:14:54,545
Now the teacher doesn't even know
whether to praise her

229
00:14:54,625 --> 00:14:55,465
or scold her.

230
00:14:55,545 --> 00:14:57,185
<i>He Xiaohe skipped school</i>
<i>five days this week.</i>

231
00:14:57,265 --> 00:14:59,305
<i>Her total score didn't even reach 95.</i>

232
00:14:59,385 --> 00:15:01,065
I'm so sorry, Mr. Zhang.

233
00:15:01,585 --> 00:15:02,945
Please calm down. I'll handle it.

234
00:15:03,025 --> 00:15:03,865
I'll deal with it right away.

235
00:15:05,305 --> 00:15:07,785
Xiaohe is brain and brawn.

236
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:11,385
She might turn out to be
a great criminal investigator.

237
00:15:16,545 --> 00:15:18,825
She's good for the physical side.

238
00:15:18,905 --> 00:15:20,345
I've trained her myself
since she was little.

239
00:15:20,425 --> 00:15:22,505
She's even better than you.

240
00:15:23,785 --> 00:15:25,105
But academically…

241
00:15:26,585 --> 00:15:27,945
Ninety-five in every subject?

242
00:15:28,865 --> 00:15:29,945
Yeah, 95 in every subject.

243
00:15:39,585 --> 00:15:40,545
Ninety-five in every subject…

244
00:15:40,625 --> 00:15:41,865
Sir.

245
00:15:43,305 --> 00:15:45,505
-Disability allowance for this month.
-I don't want it.

246
00:15:46,105 --> 00:15:48,065
The label doesn't feel right.
Taking it feels wrong.

247
00:15:48,145 --> 00:15:49,585
Disability allowance.

248
00:15:49,665 --> 00:15:51,345
It reminds me every month
that I'm disabled.

249
00:15:52,505 --> 00:15:54,345
When can I return to the team?

250
00:15:55,545 --> 00:15:57,945
You're not fully recovered yet.

251
00:15:58,465 --> 00:16:01,065
Besides, you haven't been idle.

252
00:16:01,665 --> 00:16:04,505
I know you've been looking into Xu Meng.

253
00:16:16,265 --> 00:16:18,065
I'm injured now.

254
00:16:19,025 --> 00:16:20,665
There's nothing else I can do.

255
00:16:20,745 --> 00:16:22,785
I might as well see this case through

256
00:16:23,785 --> 00:16:25,825
and give myself some closure.

257
00:16:30,905 --> 00:16:32,465
The Yuanlongli case

258
00:16:32,985 --> 00:16:34,145
feels like it's done,

259
00:16:35,025 --> 00:16:36,625
but not really.

260
00:16:38,345 --> 00:16:40,585
Feels like something's
still hanging over it.

261
00:16:42,545 --> 00:16:44,705
That's why I want to dig deeper.

262
00:16:44,785 --> 00:16:47,585
I found out Xu Meng had a boyfriend

263
00:16:47,665 --> 00:16:49,465
named Wan Qiming.

264
00:16:50,745 --> 00:16:53,345
This man is suspicious.

265
00:16:53,425 --> 00:16:55,625
I'm planning to head out of town
and meet him.

266
00:16:56,305 --> 00:16:59,105
-Out of town?
-You don't have to come with me.

267
00:16:59,865 --> 00:17:02,625
You're the captain.
You have plenty on your plate.

268
00:17:02,705 --> 00:17:05,985
If I find anything, I'll keep you posted.

269
00:17:18,985 --> 00:17:20,105
Captain,

270
00:17:20,184 --> 00:17:23,105
this is Luandongzi's statement.
Take a look.

271
00:17:23,184 --> 00:17:24,785
-Did he talk?
-He did.

272
00:17:25,625 --> 00:17:26,505
Not just that,

273
00:17:27,665 --> 00:17:29,305
he took all the blame.

274
00:17:29,385 --> 00:17:30,865
He didn't mention anything
about his accomplices.

275
00:17:33,025 --> 00:17:34,665
We worked this hard to bring him in.

276
00:17:34,745 --> 00:17:37,745
If he keeps his mouth shut,
we'll never get the others.

277
00:17:49,185 --> 00:17:50,025
The cop takes out a knife.

278
00:17:54,025 --> 00:17:55,065
You scared me.

279
00:17:58,185 --> 00:17:59,065
Captain Ran.

280
00:18:20,625 --> 00:18:22,105
I heard you confessed to everything.

281
00:18:23,065 --> 00:18:24,465
Captain Ran,

282
00:18:24,545 --> 00:18:27,905
well, I like coming clean. Come clean.

283
00:18:35,105 --> 00:18:37,905
You took 1.5 million in cash
from the Railway Administration

284
00:18:39,425 --> 00:18:40,785
all alone?

285
00:18:40,865 --> 00:18:43,745
That's right.
I brought it out all by myself.

286
00:18:45,145 --> 00:18:47,185
The compound is huge.

287
00:18:47,265 --> 00:18:51,425
Four security teams.
Patrols every five minutes.

288
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:54,745
How did you get out
carrying all that cash?

289
00:18:56,185 --> 00:18:57,785
I just saw my chance and took it.

290
00:18:57,865 --> 00:19:00,265
There happened to be
a heavy downpour that day.

291
00:19:00,345 --> 00:19:01,785
It really covered for me.

292
00:19:01,865 --> 00:19:03,425
Goodness.

293
00:19:06,465 --> 00:19:08,185
Don't get worked up.

294
00:19:09,665 --> 00:19:12,785
Yesterday, you shouted that you wanted
to report Qian Dajun from Yuanlongli.

295
00:19:12,865 --> 00:19:14,025
What's that about?

296
00:19:14,585 --> 00:19:16,545
I was talking nonsense.

297
00:19:16,625 --> 00:19:19,025
You know my line of work.

298
00:19:19,105 --> 00:19:20,265
High pressure.

299
00:19:20,345 --> 00:19:23,545
Sometimes you have to let it out.

300
00:19:29,265 --> 00:19:31,225
Come. Let's go out.

301
00:19:34,385 --> 00:19:35,465
INTERROGATION ROOM

302
00:19:38,745 --> 00:19:40,025
Let your pressure out.

303
00:19:40,105 --> 00:19:41,105
Take him out.

304
00:19:44,505 --> 00:19:46,345
Didn't you hear? Let my pressure out.

305
00:19:47,425 --> 00:19:48,825
Jeez. Let your pressure out?

306
00:19:49,625 --> 00:19:51,545
Cops can't hit just anyone.

307
00:19:52,625 --> 00:19:53,545
Hands.

308
00:20:00,705 --> 00:20:01,545
Captain Ran.

309
00:20:07,265 --> 00:20:08,865
Let's say you're telling the truth.

310
00:20:08,945 --> 00:20:10,865
The distance from
the Railway Administration building

311
00:20:10,945 --> 00:20:13,185
to the back gate is 1,400 meters.

312
00:20:13,905 --> 00:20:16,025
The perimeter of this field is 86 meters.

313
00:20:16,625 --> 00:20:19,585
Divide 1,400 by 86, it's about 16 laps.

314
00:20:19,665 --> 00:20:22,585
1.5 million in cash is under 20 kilograms.

315
00:20:23,345 --> 00:20:25,345
This bag of rice is 15 kilograms.

316
00:20:25,865 --> 00:20:27,385
Here.

317
00:20:27,465 --> 00:20:29,905
Carry it. Run 15 laps.

318
00:20:30,745 --> 00:20:34,385
I'll time you. Let's see if you can
dodge patrols within five minutes.

319
00:20:34,465 --> 00:20:36,425
-Wait.
-Come. I'll keep time.

320
00:20:36,945 --> 00:20:38,225
Ready.

321
00:20:38,305 --> 00:20:39,625
-We'll run with you.
-Ready.

322
00:20:39,705 --> 00:20:41,625
-Listen to me.
-Run.

323
00:20:43,585 --> 00:20:45,185
-Faster.
-Run.

324
00:20:45,265 --> 00:20:46,985
-Pick it up.
-Move it.

325
00:20:47,065 --> 00:20:48,345
-Speed up.
-Faster.

326
00:20:48,425 --> 00:20:50,145
-Speed up.
-Faster.

327
00:20:51,225 --> 00:20:53,105
Faster.

328
00:20:53,185 --> 00:20:55,065
Keep going.

329
00:20:55,145 --> 00:20:56,825
Speed up.

330
00:20:56,905 --> 00:20:58,105
-Faster.
-Thank you.

331
00:21:08,345 --> 00:21:10,505
-One minute and 30 seconds.
-Not even two minutes yet.

332
00:21:10,585 --> 00:21:12,065
Security hasn't come around.

333
00:21:12,145 --> 00:21:13,185
Keep running.

334
00:21:13,265 --> 00:21:14,865
-As fast as you can.
-Get up.

335
00:21:16,705 --> 00:21:17,905
I'll talk.

336
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:19,065
I'll tell you everything.

337
00:21:19,665 --> 00:21:20,825
Not just me,

338
00:21:21,345 --> 00:21:22,345
there were three others.

339
00:21:22,945 --> 00:21:25,785
Including me, there were four in total.

340
00:21:26,465 --> 00:21:27,705
Here. Wipe your face.

341
00:21:29,425 --> 00:21:30,745
Thank you.

342
00:21:35,025 --> 00:21:38,265
-Tell me about Qian Dajun.
-Right.

343
00:21:39,225 --> 00:21:42,625
There's an underground garage
in Yuanlongli, you know?

344
00:21:43,545 --> 00:21:45,985
That money grabber has a stash down there.

345
00:21:46,065 --> 00:21:48,225
A lot of valuables.

346
00:21:52,785 --> 00:21:53,945
Officer Ran,

347
00:21:54,785 --> 00:21:56,865
what are you doing
in the underground garage?

348
00:21:56,945 --> 00:21:58,105
<i>I saw it with my own eyes.</i>

349
00:21:58,185 --> 00:21:59,825
He carried a safe inside.

350
00:21:59,905 --> 00:22:01,265
When he came out,

351
00:22:01,785 --> 00:22:03,625
the safe was gone.

352
00:22:04,225 --> 00:22:06,225
I believe something's off for sure.

353
00:22:17,745 --> 00:22:18,585
Mr. Qian,

354
00:22:19,105 --> 00:22:21,105
aren't you opening up slots
for rental next month?

355
00:22:21,745 --> 00:22:24,185
Could you maybe squeeze us in early?

356
00:22:24,265 --> 00:22:27,505
MANAGER'S OFFICE

357
00:22:27,585 --> 00:22:28,185
CHUNGHWA CIGARETTE

358
00:22:34,865 --> 00:22:37,065
Officer Ran. How may I help?

359
00:22:38,745 --> 00:22:40,465
Carry on. I'll wait outside.

360
00:22:41,145 --> 00:22:42,385
Alright.

361
00:22:44,865 --> 00:22:45,705
What do you mean?

362
00:22:46,225 --> 00:22:48,585
Cut the line? That's not happening.

363
00:22:48,665 --> 00:22:50,745
The management team follows the rules.

364
00:22:51,265 --> 00:22:52,625
Take it away. Everything.

365
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:54,105
-Mr. Qian.
-Remember this.

366
00:22:54,185 --> 00:22:56,465
Handle everything by the book.
Open and transparent.

367
00:22:56,545 --> 00:22:57,985
No backdoor dealings.

368
00:22:58,505 --> 00:23:00,425
-Got it.
-Officer Ran.

369
00:23:00,505 --> 00:23:02,025
ROAD WORK AHEAD, STAY SAFE

370
00:23:07,465 --> 00:23:08,585
Officer Ran.

371
00:23:09,185 --> 00:23:10,065
Look,

372
00:23:11,465 --> 00:23:14,425
there's nothing here. Just consumables.

373
00:23:23,385 --> 00:23:25,425
Really. It's nothing.

374
00:23:26,025 --> 00:23:27,225
All junk.

375
00:23:33,265 --> 00:23:35,105
Officer Ran, these are just empty boxes.

376
00:23:35,185 --> 00:23:36,465
Just…

377
00:23:47,905 --> 00:23:49,025
Open it.

378
00:23:52,265 --> 00:23:53,985
It's been here too long.

379
00:23:54,065 --> 00:23:55,345
I forgot the passcode.

380
00:23:57,065 --> 00:23:57,905
Forgot?

381
00:24:00,665 --> 00:24:02,385
Then you and the boxes can come with me.

382
00:24:03,545 --> 00:24:04,985
I remember. I remember.

383
00:24:05,065 --> 00:24:05,905
I remember now.

384
00:24:30,305 --> 00:24:31,345
Where's the thing?

385
00:24:32,905 --> 00:24:33,745
What thing?

386
00:24:36,345 --> 00:24:40,345
Qian Dajun, someone reported you
for embezzling public assets.

387
00:24:40,425 --> 00:24:42,625
Officer Ran, I'm innocent.

388
00:24:42,705 --> 00:24:45,265
These… These are all
discarded supplies and consumables

389
00:24:45,345 --> 00:24:46,705
from the property office.

390
00:24:46,785 --> 00:24:49,385
I just wanted to sell them off
for a little cash.

391
00:24:58,945 --> 00:25:00,305
Mr. Qian,

392
00:25:00,905 --> 00:25:02,705
a word to the wise.

393
00:25:02,785 --> 00:25:04,705
Taking advantage can cost you big.

394
00:25:04,785 --> 00:25:06,225
Yes. Right.

395
00:25:06,305 --> 00:25:08,625
Don't worry. I'll make
all this disappear. Right away.

396
00:26:25,505 --> 00:26:27,465
-Hello.
-Hello.

397
00:26:27,985 --> 00:26:29,145
This man with glasses.

398
00:26:29,225 --> 00:26:30,905
Is he a photographer here?

399
00:26:30,985 --> 00:26:32,505
His style is unique.

400
00:26:33,145 --> 00:26:35,225
He's not just the photographer,
he owns this place.

401
00:26:35,305 --> 00:26:36,265
I see.

402
00:26:37,545 --> 00:26:38,545
Is he a local?

403
00:26:38,625 --> 00:26:41,625
Why are so many of his photos
taken by the sea?

404
00:26:41,705 --> 00:26:43,665
He used to work in Guangdong.

405
00:26:43,745 --> 00:26:45,665
Only came back last year
to open this place.

406
00:26:48,185 --> 00:26:49,345
This one.

407
00:26:50,345 --> 00:26:51,785
Guangdong's phone number.

408
00:26:56,625 --> 00:26:58,985
Well. I'm from a magazine.

409
00:26:59,065 --> 00:27:01,225
I really like his style.

410
00:27:01,305 --> 00:27:04,065
Could I talk to him
about a possible collaboration?

411
00:27:04,145 --> 00:27:06,505
Bad timing. He's out of town on a shoot.

412
00:27:06,585 --> 00:27:07,745
I see.

413
00:27:08,305 --> 00:27:09,145
When will he be back?

414
00:27:09,945 --> 00:27:11,225
Hard to say.

415
00:27:13,025 --> 00:27:15,345
If you need this,
you can try calling his mobile.

416
00:27:15,425 --> 00:27:17,945
But when he's out on field trips,
he usually keeps his phone off.

417
00:27:18,025 --> 00:27:19,345
Alright. Thank you.

418
00:27:19,865 --> 00:27:21,065
WAN QIMING'S BUSINESS CARD

419
00:27:55,265 --> 00:27:56,145
Sorry.

420
00:27:56,225 --> 00:27:57,625
This is Mr. Wan's private workspace.

421
00:27:57,705 --> 00:27:59,305
-Not open to visitors.
-Right.

422
00:27:59,385 --> 00:28:00,985
It does look quite unique inside.

423
00:28:01,065 --> 00:28:02,705
Mr. Wan has a wide range of interests.

424
00:28:02,785 --> 00:28:06,465
He collects antique knives.
He loves making specimens.

425
00:28:09,385 --> 00:28:11,025
Where did he go for his field trip?

426
00:28:17,145 --> 00:28:21,025
CAROUSEL'S DEAD HEAT

427
00:28:41,585 --> 00:28:43,785
SPINNING CAROUSEL

428
00:28:48,905 --> 00:28:49,785
Xiaohe.

429
00:28:49,865 --> 00:28:52,425
-Xiaohe is here.
-Look who's here.

430
00:28:52,505 --> 00:28:54,265
-Say hi.
-Officer Ran, hello.

431
00:28:55,065 --> 00:28:56,425
Hello, guys.

432
00:28:57,145 --> 00:28:59,145
Same as usual.
I'll pick you up in two hours.

433
00:29:00,065 --> 00:29:01,105
You're not staying to watch the rehearsal?

434
00:29:01,705 --> 00:29:04,705
I have plans. Record it.
I'll listen later at home.

435
00:29:06,505 --> 00:29:09,665
You guys go ahead. Wait.

436
00:29:10,505 --> 00:29:13,065
Uncle Ran, you're going on a date, right?

437
00:29:13,145 --> 00:29:15,065
I saw you texting in the car just now.

438
00:29:15,145 --> 00:29:16,625
You were blushing.

439
00:29:19,265 --> 00:29:21,665
You don't show up empty-handed for a date.

440
00:29:27,985 --> 00:29:28,945
Ms. Qiao will like it.

441
00:29:29,865 --> 00:29:31,425
It's not that.

442
00:29:31,505 --> 00:29:33,505
Uncle Ran, trust me.

443
00:29:33,585 --> 00:29:36,665
I've watched way more dramas
than cases you've worked on.

444
00:29:36,745 --> 00:29:37,585
Take it.

445
00:29:38,465 --> 00:29:39,745
Take it.

446
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:08,545
Welcome.

447
00:30:15,225 --> 00:30:16,265
Have you been waiting long?

448
00:30:17,905 --> 00:30:19,025
I just got here.

449
00:30:28,625 --> 00:30:31,305
I picked this cake up on the way just now.

450
00:30:31,385 --> 00:30:32,585
It's for you.

451
00:30:36,105 --> 00:30:37,345
Thank you.

452
00:30:48,225 --> 00:30:49,585
This is

453
00:30:50,145 --> 00:30:51,665
for me?

454
00:30:52,745 --> 00:30:53,585
Yes.

455
00:30:56,825 --> 00:30:57,705
It's from Xiaohe.

456
00:30:58,985 --> 00:31:00,745
I just brought it over.

457
00:31:09,985 --> 00:31:11,025
Thank you.

458
00:31:27,785 --> 00:31:28,745
<i>Freedom, freedom</i>

459
00:31:28,825 --> 00:31:31,145
<i>It's burning</i>

460
00:31:31,225 --> 00:31:34,465
<i>Close your eyes, get some rest</i>

461
00:31:34,545 --> 00:31:35,385
<i>Run, run</i>

462
00:31:37,505 --> 00:31:39,065
What the heck is this?

463
00:31:39,145 --> 00:31:40,465
Who did this?

464
00:31:40,545 --> 00:31:41,665
Come out here.

465
00:31:41,745 --> 00:31:43,985
-Who turned on the light? Come out here.
-Come out!

466
00:31:48,265 --> 00:31:49,145
Dad.

467
00:31:49,225 --> 00:31:50,705
Why are you back?

468
00:31:52,705 --> 00:31:54,305
My dear son,

469
00:31:54,865 --> 00:31:56,345
you really didn't disappoint me.

470
00:31:56,425 --> 00:31:57,465
Dad, let me explain.

471
00:31:57,545 --> 00:31:58,625
Explain it to my belt.

472
00:31:58,705 --> 00:32:00,745
-Stand right there! Stand right there!
-Dad.

473
00:32:00,825 --> 00:32:01,945
-I was wrong.
-Stop!

474
00:32:02,025 --> 00:32:03,265
-You're still running?
-Run.

475
00:32:03,345 --> 00:32:04,225
Don't run.

476
00:32:04,785 --> 00:32:06,665
Stand right there. Don't run!

477
00:32:07,665 --> 00:32:08,905
Run.

478
00:32:11,585 --> 00:32:13,585
Not this way. The door's locked. Go.

479
00:32:17,505 --> 00:32:18,225
Why are you running?

480
00:32:20,265 --> 00:32:21,425
Where's the other girl?

481
00:32:44,385 --> 00:32:45,465
Your guitar looks cool.

482
00:32:47,025 --> 00:32:49,705
Mister, where did you get it?

483
00:32:49,785 --> 00:32:51,105
You can't buy this anywhere.

484
00:33:01,985 --> 00:33:04,865
<i>The summer solstice wind</i>
<i>Still blows at dusk</i>

485
00:33:06,225 --> 00:33:08,465
<i>It passes the moon</i>

486
00:33:08,545 --> 00:33:11,025
<i>Tracing the brows</i>

487
00:33:12,985 --> 00:33:16,025
<i>The world under the moon is bustling</i>

488
00:33:17,225 --> 00:33:19,265
<i>Yet I have no idea</i>

489
00:33:19,345 --> 00:33:21,425
<i>Where I should go</i>

490
00:33:24,025 --> 00:33:26,465
<i>Oh, youth</i>

491
00:33:26,545 --> 00:33:29,265
<i>So dazzling, so vast</i>

492
00:33:29,345 --> 00:33:31,905
<i>Dreams fill a young heart</i>

493
00:33:31,985 --> 00:33:36,905
<i>Yet they're beyond reach</i>

494
00:33:46,065 --> 00:33:48,065
Teach me that.
I'll take you as my teacher.

495
00:33:49,185 --> 00:33:52,465
I'm leaving Weiyang tomorrow
for another city.

496
00:33:53,065 --> 00:33:55,705
Busking? I'll go with you.

497
00:33:55,785 --> 00:33:57,545
That's one man's adventure.

498
00:34:00,345 --> 00:34:01,385
Girl,

499
00:34:01,905 --> 00:34:03,625
if you really want to learn,

500
00:34:03,705 --> 00:34:04,625
go to Beijing.

501
00:34:04,705 --> 00:34:06,625
That's where rock started in China.

502
00:34:10,824 --> 00:34:12,025
Beijing?

503
00:34:16,425 --> 00:34:18,304
I'm planning to move next week

504
00:34:18,385 --> 00:34:20,824
to somewhere closer to work.

505
00:34:20,905 --> 00:34:22,505
I'm sharing a place with others.

506
00:34:26,985 --> 00:34:28,185
Don't rush.

507
00:34:28,264 --> 00:34:30,585
The unit just assigned me an apartment.

508
00:34:30,665 --> 00:34:33,945
I'm alone and used to the dorm.
I don't need it.

509
00:34:34,025 --> 00:34:36,344
If you don't mind, you can move in.

510
00:34:36,985 --> 00:34:38,744
I can't do that.

511
00:34:38,824 --> 00:34:40,705
It's assigned to you. It's not appropriate

512
00:34:40,784 --> 00:34:42,985
-for me to move in.
-It's fine.

513
00:34:43,065 --> 00:34:44,505
You've been living alone.

514
00:34:44,585 --> 00:34:47,225
You won't get used to sharing.

515
00:34:49,264 --> 00:34:50,945
Thank you, Ran.

516
00:34:51,025 --> 00:34:52,065
But no.

517
00:34:57,025 --> 00:34:58,425
Honestly,

518
00:34:59,025 --> 00:35:00,545
as long as there's no ghost,

519
00:35:01,385 --> 00:35:03,185
a little discomfort

520
00:35:03,825 --> 00:35:05,345
doesn't matter.

521
00:35:12,465 --> 00:35:15,865
That old man gave me food,

522
00:35:16,785 --> 00:35:17,785
money,

523
00:35:19,105 --> 00:35:20,745
and a place to stay.

524
00:35:22,545 --> 00:35:23,665
But

525
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:29,665
he never gave me dignity.

526
00:35:37,745 --> 00:35:39,465
<i>He was weak and afraid of light.</i>

527
00:35:40,305 --> 00:35:43,425
<i>Not a single ray of sunlight</i>
<i>was allowed inside.</i>

528
00:35:45,025 --> 00:35:46,465
You trying to burn me?

529
00:35:52,385 --> 00:35:53,385
<i>Back then,</i>

530
00:35:55,465 --> 00:35:57,705
<i>I never slept well</i>

531
00:35:59,105 --> 00:36:00,945
<i>or had a proper meal.</i>

532
00:36:06,745 --> 00:36:07,905
Come here.

533
00:36:12,145 --> 00:36:13,305
Faster.

534
00:36:15,545 --> 00:36:16,825
Wipe it.

535
00:36:27,265 --> 00:36:28,385
You trollop.

536
00:36:36,065 --> 00:36:37,105
Did you try to put me to sleep?

537
00:36:37,905 --> 00:36:39,505
Did you? Did you?

538
00:36:39,585 --> 00:36:40,945
-You want me…
-No!

539
00:36:41,025 --> 00:36:42,385
asleep all the time?

540
00:36:42,465 --> 00:36:43,305
Right?

541
00:36:51,825 --> 00:36:53,625
He treated you like that.

542
00:36:54,145 --> 00:36:56,105
Why did you stay and take care of him?

543
00:36:57,385 --> 00:37:00,905
He had a bad temper
and drove off every caretaker.

544
00:37:00,985 --> 00:37:02,665
No one else would take the job.

545
00:37:03,185 --> 00:37:05,785
So the pay was high.

546
00:37:06,705 --> 00:37:08,945
My mom had just passed.

547
00:37:09,545 --> 00:37:11,825
I was buried in debt.

548
00:37:12,425 --> 00:37:15,785
I couldn't find anything that paid better.

549
00:37:22,145 --> 00:37:23,265
Qiao.

550
00:37:24,145 --> 00:37:26,345
You were miserable at Yuanlongli.

551
00:37:26,945 --> 00:37:28,025
After he died,

552
00:37:28,705 --> 00:37:30,065
why didn't you move out?

553
00:37:31,105 --> 00:37:33,065
His son's overseas.

554
00:37:33,145 --> 00:37:35,505
He asked me to watch the place,

555
00:37:35,585 --> 00:37:36,825
and it's rent-free.

556
00:37:37,425 --> 00:37:39,665
But he's coming back soon.

557
00:37:41,585 --> 00:37:44,385
Ran, I'm not trying to take advantage.

558
00:37:44,985 --> 00:37:46,625
I've wanted to move out for a while.

559
00:37:47,465 --> 00:37:48,345
It's just…

560
00:37:56,345 --> 00:37:59,105
I thought maybe

561
00:37:59,905 --> 00:38:03,305
I'd run into you again if I stayed there.

562
00:38:11,225 --> 00:38:13,145
Qiao, I…

563
00:38:15,905 --> 00:38:18,385
Ran, don't be nervous.

564
00:38:19,945 --> 00:38:21,785
I know I'm not good enough for you.

565
00:38:21,865 --> 00:38:23,785
I… No.

566
00:38:25,545 --> 00:38:27,265
That's not what I meant.

567
00:38:28,825 --> 00:38:31,665
Saying this out loud

568
00:38:32,545 --> 00:38:34,305
makes me feel better.

569
00:38:44,785 --> 00:38:50,305
YUNSHAN ZIZHU RESTAURANT

570
00:38:58,185 --> 00:39:00,665
It's cold out here. I can give you a ride.

571
00:39:00,745 --> 00:39:01,985
No need.

572
00:39:02,065 --> 00:39:04,665
The office is around here. I'll just walk.

573
00:39:05,185 --> 00:39:06,465
You should get back to work.

574
00:39:09,585 --> 00:39:10,905
Hey.

575
00:39:12,745 --> 00:39:14,585
-Are you alright?
-I'm fine.

576
00:39:16,585 --> 00:39:18,705
It's okay. You don't
have to keep the flower.

577
00:39:19,825 --> 00:39:20,665
No.

578
00:39:21,905 --> 00:39:23,705
You gave it to me.

579
00:39:23,785 --> 00:39:25,105
I won't let it get dirty.

580
00:40:12,825 --> 00:40:13,785
Step back a bit.

581
00:40:13,865 --> 00:40:15,025
The ambulance is coming.

582
00:40:15,105 --> 00:40:16,345
Make way.

583
00:40:20,745 --> 00:40:21,865
Back up.

584
00:40:24,985 --> 00:40:26,585
Back up.

585
00:40:29,305 --> 00:40:31,585
Look. A kid died in the fire.

586
00:40:31,665 --> 00:40:32,905
Choked on the smoke. Didn't make it out.

587
00:40:33,865 --> 00:40:35,745
Make way. Make way.

588
00:40:35,825 --> 00:40:37,185
Make way. Ran Fangxu from Nanshan Branch.

589
00:40:38,425 --> 00:40:39,425
AMBULANCE

